      ],
      "concerns": "Verified by unit-scout: MarkFlagsRequiredTogether/OneRequired/MutuallyExclusive have no non-test in-repo callers but are the intended public API for external CLI authors, so they are kept as entrypoints. ValidateFlagGroups is called from command.go:1010; enforceFlagGroupsForCompletion is called from completions.go:433 - both confirmed."
    },
    {
      "name": "flag-completion-annotations",
      "kind": "domain",
      "description": "This unit lets a CLI author (or another part of Cobra) attach a small piece of extra meaning to one flag: 'this flag's value should be a filename with one of these extensions', 'this flag's value should be a directory name', 'this flag is required so prioritize suggesting it', or 'call this custom shell function to complete this flag's value'. It does no rendering and no file I/O itself - it only records these hints as annotations on the flag, for the shell-script generators and the completion engine to read back later when they decide what to suggest.",
