    {
      "name": "completion-engine",
      "kind": "domain",
      "description": "This unit defines what 'tab completion' means inside a Cobra-based command-line program, independent of which shell (bash, zsh, fish, PowerShell) the user is typing into. It provides a hidden internal command that any generated shell script calls behind the scenes to ask 'what are the valid choices right now?', walks the program's command and flag tree to figure out the answer, lets the program's author register custom suggestion logic for specific flags or arguments, supports attaching short 'active help' hint messages to suggestions, and lets the program's author or its users tweak completion behavior (such as turning off descriptions or hints) through environment variables. The actual shell-specific script text that wires this into bash/zsh/fish/PowerShell lives elsewhere; this unit is the shell-agnostic rulebook those scripts call into.",
      "files": ["completions.go", "active_help.go"],
